# idct-mmx-saturation-probe.meta
source_path: video/msmpeg4/reference/binaries/wmpcdcs8-2001/mpg4c32.dll
source_sha256: aedb4cf3d33c8554ab8acf04afe2d936eaa7c49107c5fefe163bca2e94b3c099
tool: ud-emulator (univdreams 3f43799, x87 RC-field fix) round27_msmpeg4_watch harness; provenance/sandbox-04
  (first captured in round 27 / sandbox-03 on univdreams 539f04e, regenerated in round 28 — see history below)
input: provenance/sandbox-03/inputs/iframe-sat.bin (hand-built 32x16 MP43 I-frame, PQUANT 31,
  coefficients carried by the TCOEF escape fixed-length arm; builder tools/mkiframe.py)
method: read-watch on the decoder's int32 coefficient buffer (this+0x5a4, 256 bytes) and
  write-watch on the picture planes while the MMX put IDCT 0x1c22a039 ran; the 64 input
  coefficients and the 64 output samples of the two coded luma blocks were captured.
kind: idct_test_vector
columns: block, kind, c<r>_<k> (dequantised coefficient at natural row r column k, i.e. the
  transpose of the decoder's memory buffer, which is stored transposed under the MMX build),
  p<r>_<k> (output sample written to the picture at row r column k)
semantics: these two blocks are reproduced pixel-exactly by the int16/23-bit MMX model
  (provenance/27 §1.4; tools/idct_check.py idct_mmx_model) and NOT by the int32 scalar
  arithmetic of provenance/26 §1.3 (28 and 22 of 64 samples differ). They pin the MMX
  pair as the arithmetic the sandbox reference decodes use. Coefficient magnitudes of
  this size are only reachable through the escape fixed-length arm (8-bit level at
  PQUANT 31); no vendor-encoded frame traced so far reaches them.
csv_sha256: 4a34c269417c9e3901d8a19d2f3e2e975201fe610bdf7547c7ae0af32bd0dd98
history: the round-27 capture (csv_sha256 05f30f1040813207560ef277b012813a3e42b4e538a3aa528cd4f9e12c7cfeea)
  was taken on an emulator whose FISTP ignored the truncate control word, so its block DC
  (c0_0 = 1058 = 23*46) came from a default DC of 23 instead of the hardware value 22; both
  blocks now carry c0_0 = 1012 (= 22*46) and the corresponding output samples (block 0 row 0
  is 44 168 255 255 0 0 85 0; it was 44 174 255 255 0 0 91 0). The MMX model reproduces both
  versions 0/64 and the scalar arithmetic misses 28/64 and 21/64 in both; only this version
  is what a real CPU produces from inputs/iframe-sat.bin. Source: provenance/28 §2, sandbox-04
  traces/esc-sat2.trace.jsonl.
verdict: pass (behavioural, hardware-grade after the RC fix)
